File-type icons in this directory
=================================

The SVGs in this folder are taken from the **vscode-icons** project
(https://github.com/vscode-icons/vscode-icons), released under the MIT
license. They are copied verbatim; the plugin only renames nothing, it maps
file extensions to these files in `assets/userfiles.js` and ships them as
static assets.

Chosen subset (23): pdf, word, excel, powerpoint, text, markdown, zip, audio,
video, image, photoshop, php, js, typescript, css, html, json, xml, sql,
python, csv, android, binary.

The rest of the icon set is not bundled: a format without an icon falls back
to the plugin's own text chip (`assets/userfiles.js` → `fileMark()`), so
adding one later is a matter of dropping the SVG here and adding a mapping.

